    {
      "id": "03-create",
      "instruction": "In Odoo, go to the Sales app and create a new quotation (Sales > Orders > Quotations > New). Set the Customer field to '{{runid}} Bench Customer' — it is an autocomplete dropdown, so type the name and actually select the matching option from the dropdown. Then add exactly ONE order line: pick any product from the product catalogue (again via the autocomplete dropdown, selecting an actual option), set its quantity to 3. Let Odoo fill in the unit price automatically. Save the quotation. Then report: (a) the product name you chose, (b) the unit price the app filled in on that line, (c) the Untaxed Amount shown in the quotation's totals, and (d) the quotation's reference/name (e.g. S00042). Do not wait for network idle — wait on concrete page state instead.",
      "outputs": [
        "product_name",
        "quantity",
        "unit_price",
        "line_tax_excl",
        "taxes",
        "customer",
        "customer_city_shown",
        "quotation_reference",
        "record_saved",
        "final_url"
      ],
